      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.84,
          "end": 5.84,
          "en": "So, what is NextJS and why would you use it?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 6.63,
          "end": 11.63,
          "en": "Well, the answer is NextJS is a React framework,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 12.12,
          "end": 15.75,
          "en": "so it builds up on React.js,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 15.75,
          "end": 18.3,
          "en": "and you therefore, of course, might wonder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 18.3,
          "end": 20.07,
          "en": "why do we need it?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 20.07,
          "end": 24.66,
          "en": "After all, React.js is already a library itself.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 24.66,
          "end": 26.88,
          "en": "Why do we need another framework",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 26.88,
          "end": 30.66,
          "en": "that builds up on React.js?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 30.66,
          "end": 35.66,
          "en": "Well, because NextJS is a full stack React framework,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 36.75,
          "end": 39.36,
          "en": "so it simplifies the process",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 39.36,
          "end": 42.84,
          "en": "of building full stack apps with React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 42.84,
          "end": 45.48,
          "en": "And that's a huge thing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 45.48,
          "end": 50.4,
          "en": "because recently, over the last couple of months and years,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 50.4,
          "end": 53.61,
          "en": "there's been a trend to go back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 53.61,
          "end": 56.16,
          "en": "to building full stack applications",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 56.16,
          "end": 60.63,
          "en": "instead of just client-side single page applications.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 60.63,
          "end": 63.57,
          "en": "And indeed, the React library itself",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 63.57,
          "end": 65.67,
          "en": "added more and more features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 65.67,
          "end": 69.93,
          "en": "that make it a bit easier to run React on the server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 69.93,
          "end": 74.03999999999999,
          "en": "and render components on the server specifically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 74.03999999999999,
          "end": 76.59,
          "en": "But that's typically not all you need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 76.59,
          "end": 79.53,
          "en": "if you want to build a full stack application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 79.53,
          "end": 81.24,
          "en": "Instead, if you wanna build",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 81.24,
          "end": 85.26,
          "en": "a complete, feature-rich full stack application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 85.26,
          "end": 88.89,
          "en": "you also need help with handling form submissions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 88.89,
          "end": 91.98,
          "en": "fetching data, authenticating users,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 91.98,
          "end": 94.05,
          "en": "and a lot of other things.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 94.05,
          "end": 97.97999999999999,
          "en": "And that's exactly what NextJS gives you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 97.97999999999999,
          "end": 99.9,
          "en": "So, it builds up on React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 99.9,
          "end": 103.53,
          "en": "and then vastly simplifies the process",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 103.53,
          "end": 107.581,
          "en": "of building full stack applications with React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 107.581,
          "end": 111.27000000000001,
          "en": "Therefore, in order to use NextJS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 111.27000000000001,
          "end": 114.84,
          "en": "and in order to build applications with NextJS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 114.84,
          "end": 118.53,
          "en": "you need a solid React foundation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 118.53,
          "end": 120.21,
          "en": "You need to know React,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 120.21,
          "end": 123.81,
          "en": "because you'll still be building components and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 123.81,
          "end": 128.81,
          "en": "But then NextJS allows you to take your React skills",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 128.91,
          "end": 131.25,
          "en": "to the next level, so to say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 131.25,
          "end": 132.54,
          "en": "and it allows you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 132.54,
          "end": 135.99,
          "en": "to build full stack applications with React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 135.99,
          "end": 138.21,
          "en": "And that's exactly what we'll do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
